+/* ---- Patch 0034: frames presented when translated, vblanks locked to the display.
+ *
+ * Before: the walker parks on a translated flip until the next tick of the
+ * 59.94 Hz QPC vblank clock, the tick presents it, and the display shows it at
+ * its own next refresh -- two waits in series, ~0.5 + ~0.5 refresh on average
+ * (docs/RENDER_PERF.md "Input latency"). Now:
+ *
+ *   PS3_PRESENT_AT_XLAT (default 1): a flip is presented as soon as the walker
+ *     reaches it (translated); the guest still sees it complete on the next
+ *     vblank tick, so the game's pace is unchanged.
+ *   PS3_DISPLAY_LOCK (default 1): when the window's display runs at the game's
+ *     rate (59/60 Hz, vsync on; rsx_live_draw_display_lockable), the vblank
+ *     ticks follow the display's own vblank clock (DWM: last vblank, period):
+ *     the period becomes the display's, and the phase is set so that a tick
+ *     comes `lead` before a display vblank. A tick releases the game's next
+ *     frame (it reads the pads at its start), the frame is presented when
+ *     translated, before that vblank. `lead` follows what frames cost here
+ *     (tick -> present, 99th percentile of the last 240, + PS3_DISPLAY_MARGIN_MS,
+ *     default 1.5): up at once after two late frames, down by 1 ms a second.
